Material gaps:
- Direct 2022 evidence on Biden personally benefiting from, obstructing scrutiny of, or concealing family/business matters remains thin; the strongest material is still negative-proof style reporting rather than a direct finding.
- I still want a better 2022 primary trail on ethics waivers, financial-recusal decisions, and any OGE/DOJ actions involving the president himself rather than his relatives or appointees.
- The clearest negative pattern is repeated factual exaggeration in speeches; I do not yet have a clean, direct record of corrections or retractions that would materially strengthen 7B.2.
- More 2022-specific independent evidence on appointee vetting and disclosure compliance would help separate institutional professionalism from self-reporting.

No score.
